Author: Katherine Reilly
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-04-05
Number: 16
Notes: A 13-wide diamond with a diamond-shaped centre panel (r5c7; r6c6-8; r7c5-9; r8c6-8; r9c7, shown as _) printed "No 16"; the intro also calls it "the sixteenth in FUN'S series". Number from the centre panel. Credit as printed: "was sent in by Miss Katherine Reilly, 332 East Fifty-sixth street, New York City." Intro as printed: "Today's cross-word puzzle, the sixteenth in FUN'S series, was sent in by Miss Katherine Reilly, 332 East Fifty-sixth street, New York City. See if you can solve it. Fill in the small squares in the above diamond with words corresponding to the clews and definitions given below. On another page you will find the solution to last week's cross-word puzzle. The solution to today's puzzle will be given in next week's FUN." Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_04_05_89.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_04_12_89.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.


